==English==

===Etymology 1===
{{borrowing|la|bulla||bubble|lang=en}}.

====Noun====
{{slim-wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|bullae}}

# {{context|medicine|lang=en}} A [[blister]], [[vesicle]], or other thin-walled cavity or [[lesion]].
# {{context|archaeology|lang=en}} A clay envelope or hollow ball, typically with seal impressions or writing on its outside indicating its contents.
# {{context|historical|lang=en}} In ancient Rome, a kind of [[amulet]] or [[boss]].
# Later, a handwritten document from the papal chancellery.

