==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|cel-gau|la}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{m|ine-pro|*beu||swelling}}, same source as Middle Dutch {{m|dum|puyl||bag}} and Lithuanian {{m|lt|bule||buttocks}}.<ref>Skeat, An Etymological Dictionary of the English Language</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-pronunc|bulla}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|bulla|bullae|bullae|f|first}}

# a [[bubble]], a water bubble; any round object that has swollen
# {{context|on a door etc.|lang=la}} a [[boss]], a [[knob]]
# the [[#English|bulla]], an amulet worn upon the neck
# {{context|Ecclesiastical Latin|lang=la}} handwritten document from the pope or the papal chancellery ([[papal bull]])

